{"duration_api_ms":414704,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"5de3af7b-308a-4258-8e8f-c68c08e78212","total_cost_usd":2.1738238000000005,"usage":{"input_tokens":142,"cache_creation_input_tokens":108688,"cache_read_input_tokens":6777689,"output_tokens":38325,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":15808},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":108688,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3102,"cache_read_input_tokens":131839,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1180,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1180},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":142,"outputTokens":38325,"cacheReadInputTokens":6777689,"cacheCreationInputTokens":108688,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":2.1738238000000005,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":15808,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":107,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"Segmented node2 (VLAN 10) and node3 (VLAN 20) over their shared trunk link (node1's eth1, node2/node3's enp8s0 — a second NIC separate from the 10.100.227.0/24 management network), and configured node1 (VyOS) to route between the VLANs. Implemented entirely via Ansible run from node4, the cluster's designated control node (the only node with ansible/ansible-playbook installed). Verified with packet captures that traffic is genuinely 802.1Q-tagged and L3-routed (not bridged) through node1, confirmed VLAN isolation (untagged traffic on the shared link no longer reaches node3), and completed the mandatory one-at-a-time restart protocol on all four nodes with boot-identity proof and post-restart recovery verification.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Discovered topology: node1 (VyOS) eth1, node2/node3 (Ubuntu 24.04) enp8s0 form an isolated second-NIC shared link, confirmed by temporary IP + ping test before building the real config\",\"Fixed missing SSH host keys (ssh-keygen -A) and started sshd on node2/node3 so the Ansible control node could reach them\",\"Provisioned the cluster's shared SSH keypair (CLUSTER_SSH_PUBKEY/PRIVKEY) for control-node access: added pubkey to node2/node3 root authorized_keys, and to node1's VyOS `vyos` user via `set system login user vyos authentication public-keys`, commit+save\",\"Confirmed VyOS requires `sudo` (vyos user has NOPASSWD ALL) to run the configure/commit/save script-template envelope non-interactively over SSH; validated the exact invocation pattern before scripting it\",\"Built an Ansible project on node4 at /root/ansible/vlan-segmentation/ (inventory.ini, ansible.cfg, playbook.yml, templates/) with two plays: (1) linux_hosts play templating systemd-networkd 10-<iface>-trunk.network + vlanN.netdev + 20-vlanN.network files on node2/node3, creating tagged VLAN sub-interfaces vlan10 (node2, 10.10.10.2/24) and vlan20 (node3, 10.20.20.2/24) with static routes to the peer's subnet via node1; (2) vyos_router play templating and applying a VyOS config script creating eth1 vif 10 (10.10.10.1/24) and vif 20 (10.20.20.1/24), committed and saved\",\"Ran ansible-playbook playbook.yml successfully across all three managed nodes, then re-ran with --check to confirm idempotency\",\"Verified routing with ping (TTL=63, confirming one L3 hop through node1) and a tcpdump capture on node1's eth1 showing ICMP packets arrive tagged vlan10 and leave re-tagged vlan20 (and vice versa), proving genuine VLAN routing rather than bridging\",\"Verified VLAN isolation: a ping from node2's untagged enp8s0 (bypassing the VLAN tag) to node3 fails 100%, while the tagged vlan10 interface succeeds\",\"Captured baseline boot_id and health (interfaces, routes, ping) on all four nodes\",\"Restarted node2, then node3, then node1, then node4 one at a time via a backgrounded `sleep 2; reboot` so the ack returned before disconnection; polled each until reachable again\",\"Proved each restart via changed /proc/sys/kernel/random/boot_id (node1: 2eb8b6e8→86448709, node2: c0691b74→26f052d4, node3: 29011044→dfeb861c, node4: 6fd57414→5ccb4a0f)\",\"Verified post-restart recovery on each node: VLAN interfaces/routes still present (persisted via systemd-networkd units on Linux, VyOS config.boot save on node1), cross-VLAN ping still succeeding, and on node4 the Ansible control setup (keys, project files) intact and playbook still idempotent\",\"Cleaned up temporary files (/tmp/reboot.log, test scripts, tcpdump capture) from all nodes\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"node2 placed on VLAN 10 over the shared link\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-9ad16ddbb6d94ccd\",\"cmd-0e551a8f98a045b5\"],\"summary\":\"Ansible playbook run created vlan10@enp8s0 with 10.10.10.2/24 on node2; ip -4 addr show confirms the interface and address\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 placed on VLAN 20 over the shared link\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-9ad16ddbb6d94ccd\",\"cmd-5ee819e9fab54517\"],\"summary\":\"Ansible playbook run created vlan20@enp8s0 with 10.20.20.2/24 on node3; ip -4 addr show confirms the interface and address\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 (VyOS) configured to route between the two VLANs\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-9ad16ddbb6d94ccd\",\"cmd-6e95309842364975\"],\"summary\":\"Ansible applied eth1.10 (10.10.10.1/24) and eth1.20 (10.20.20.1/24) sub-interfaces on node1 via VyOS configure/commit/save; ip -4 addr/route confirm both are present with kernel routes\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 and node3 can still reach each other, routed via node1 (not directly bridged)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-26b44de8b16545e5\",\"cmd-96418a15d29e483b\",\"cmd-e20ac211285a46b2\",\"cmd-4b470d9f66954516\"],\"summary\":\"Ping between 10.10.10.2 and 10.20.20.2 succeeds with TTL=63 (one hop); tcpdump on node1 eth1 shows ICMP re-tagged from vlan10 to vlan20 and back, proving L3 routing; direct untagged ping on node2's enp8s0 to node3 fails, proving VLAN segmentation/isolation is real\"},{\"requirement\":\"Implementation done via Ansible from the cluster's control node\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-aacbde6d64934a33\",\"cmd-faee2ef1c82348d8\",\"cmd-9ad16ddbb6d94ccd\",\"cmd-f25d92d00fbc4983\"],\"summary\":\"node4 is the only node with ansible/ansible-playbook installed; inventory/playbook built there and ansible-playbook run (and idempotent --check re-run) executed the full configuration\"},{\"requirement\":\"Mandatory restart evidence: node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-099bab33332c45c1\",\"cmd-c50f44e0131646b9\",\"cmd-f777c1db451449c3\",\"cmd-e9b3eac3612c40ee\",\"cmd-99b9db5fc0a14104\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 2eb8b6e8...; reboot acknowledged; boot_id changed to 86448709... after poll; post-restart ip addr/route show VLAN config persisted; cross-VLAN ping from node2 still succeeds\"},{\"requirement\":\"Mandatory restart evidence: node2\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-29a8c663a9ff49bc\",\"cmd-c336ced82f8d4b00\",\"cmd-4cd90ba000614258\",\"cmd-66f27574e6ed430c\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id c0691b74...; reboot acknowledged; boot_id changed to 26f052d4... after poll; post-restart vlan10 interface, route, and ping to node3 all recovered\"},{\"requirement\":\"Mandatory restart evidence: node3\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-7e1b0f6805a84b26\",\"cmd-f66789d908134f34\",\"cmd-7afaf4776d244c7e\",\"cmd-74481a9104e4428d\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 29011044...; reboot acknowledged; boot_id changed to dfeb861c... after poll; post-restart vlan20 interface, route, and ping to node2 all recovered\"},{\"requirement\":\"Mandatory restart evidence: node4\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-f25d92d00fbc4983\",\"cmd-00e310ae558f4c94\",\"cmd-650e986f78814fb0\",\"cmd-90a1d00807394c4a\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 6fd57414...; reboot acknowledged; boot_id changed to 5ccb4a0f... after poll; post-restart Ansible project files intact and playbook --check runs cleanly (idempotent), confirming control-node functionality recovered\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Segmented node2 (VLAN 10) and node3 (VLAN 20) over their shared trunk link (node1's eth1, node2/node3's enp8s0 — a second NIC separate from the 10.100.227.0/24 management network), and configured node1 (VyOS) to route between the VLANs. Implemented entirely via Ansible run from node4, the cluster's designated control node (the only node with ansible/ansible-playbook installed). Verified with packet captures that traffic is genuinely 802.1Q-tagged and L3-routed (not bridged) through node1, confirmed VLAN isolation (untagged traffic on the shared link no longer reaches node3), and completed the mandatory one-at-a-time restart protocol on all four nodes with boot-identity proof and post-restart recovery verification.","actions_performed":["Discovered topology: node1 (VyOS) eth1, node2/node3 (Ubuntu 24.04) enp8s0 form an isolated second-NIC shared link, confirmed by temporary IP + ping test before building the real config","Fixed missing SSH host keys (ssh-keygen -A) and started sshd on node2/node3 so the Ansible control node could reach them","Provisioned the cluster's shared SSH keypair (CLUSTER_SSH_PUBKEY/PRIVKEY) for control-node access: added pubkey to node2/node3 root authorized_keys, and to node1's VyOS `vyos` user via `set system login user vyos authentication public-keys`, commit+save","Confirmed VyOS requires `sudo` (vyos user has NOPASSWD ALL) to run the configure/commit/save script-template envelope non-interactively over SSH; validated the exact invocation pattern before scripting it","Built an Ansible project on node4 at /root/ansible/vlan-segmentation/ (inventory.ini, ansible.cfg, playbook.yml, templates/) with two plays: (1) linux_hosts play templating systemd-networkd 10-<iface>-trunk.network + vlanN.netdev + 20-vlanN.network files on node2/node3, creating tagged VLAN sub-interfaces vlan10 (node2, 10.10.10.2/24) and vlan20 (node3, 10.20.20.2/24) with static routes to the peer's subnet via node1; (2) vyos_router play templating and applying a VyOS config script creating eth1 vif 10 (10.10.10.1/24) and vif 20 (10.20.20.1/24), committed and saved","Ran ansible-playbook playbook.yml successfully across all three managed nodes, then re-ran with --check to confirm idempotency","Verified routing with ping (TTL=63, confirming one L3 hop through node1) and a tcpdump capture on node1's eth1 showing ICMP packets arrive tagged vlan10 and leave re-tagged vlan20 (and vice versa), proving genuine VLAN routing rather than bridging","Verified VLAN isolation: a ping from node2's untagged enp8s0 (bypassing the VLAN tag) to node3 fails 100%, while the tagged vlan10 interface succeeds","Captured baseline boot_id and health (interfaces, routes, ping) on all four nodes","Restarted node2, then node3, then node1, then node4 one at a time via a backgrounded `sleep 2; reboot` so the ack returned before disconnection; polled each until reachable again","Proved each restart via changed /proc/sys/kernel/random/boot_id (node1: 2eb8b6e8→86448709, node2: c0691b74→26f052d4, node3: 29011044→dfeb861c, node4: 6fd57414→5ccb4a0f)","Verified post-restart recovery on each node: VLAN interfaces/routes still present (persisted via systemd-networkd units on Linux, VyOS config.boot save on node1), cross-VLAN ping still succeeding, and on node4 the Ansible control setup (keys, project files) intact and playbook still idempotent","Cleaned up temporary files (/tmp/reboot.log, test scripts, tcpdump capture) from all nodes"],"evidence":[